    "text": "The total pressure of a mixture of non-reacting gases <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>45</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></math> in a vessel is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>740</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math>&nbsp;of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Hg</mi></math>. The partial pressure of the gas <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>mm</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Hg</mi><mo>.</mo></math> (Nearest Integer)<br />(Given : molar mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>45</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> )",
